 ## Overview
-Octree-based traversal accelerates volume rendering and implicit surface rendering by recursively traversing a hierarchical spatial subdivision (typically an octree) to skip empty space and large uniform regions. It differs from flat grid traversal by using tree structure to bypass empty volumes, and from Empty-Space Skipping which uses primitive hulls, by employing hierarchical spatial subdivision to locate non-empty space faster [S1]. It sets itself apart from its siblings, such as [Octree Partitioning for Sphere Tracing](1541-octree-partitioning-for-sphere-tracing.md), by using explicit bounds tracking and entry/exit side tracking with a callback for leaf processing rather than fixed-step iteration [S2, unofficial].
